# Line endings are not cosmetic in this repository - two file types break outright if git rewrites
# them on checkout, and core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) will do exactly that.

# Normalise everything to LF in the repository and on checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell hooks MUST be LF. With CRLF the shebang becomes "#!/usr/bin/env bash\r", the kernel looks for
# an interpreter literally named "bash\r", and every bash hook dies with "bad interpreter: No such
# file or directory". Nothing in the acceptance test catches this because it only appears after a
# clone on a machine with autocrlf enabled - which is every Windows machine by default.
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell hook scripts are pure ASCII with a UTF-8 BOM - Windows PowerShell 5.1, which the Copilot
# host uses, reads BOM-less files as cp1252 and mojibake breaks string terminators. Git does not
# touch the BOM, but pin the endings so a clone matches the bytes that were actually tested.
*.ps1 text eol=lf

# Never convert these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.gif binary
